+/* RIG (coordinator only): upstream hardwires this to `#if 1`, so the COOJA
+ * SIMULATOR compensation is always on.  On real hardware it makes
+ * backoff_period 6 ms instead of aUnitBackoffPeriod (320 us), and with
+ * CSMA_MAX_BE that is up to rand(0,255)*6 ms for a single retry -- which is
+ * what limited this network to about 1 message/s.  The coordinator is the
+ * traffic source and needs the standard value; the VICTIM is left untouched,
+ * because its soft ACK is a direct NETSTACK_RADIO.send that never goes
+ * through csma_output at all. */
